@@ -0,0 +1,70 @@
+# Passkeys API contract (My Account)
+
+`js/account.js` calls these same-origin endpoints with cookie sessions. All
+WebAuthn options and responses use the standard WebAuthn JSON encoding
+(Base64URL, no padding). On the server, use a vetted library such as
+[SimpleWebAuthn](https://github.com/MasterKale/SimpleWebAuthn) to generate options and
+verify responses. Don't hand-roll the crypto.
+
+`RP_ID` is a fixed server constant (for example `dailygrind.example`). The client
+never works out the RP ID from `location.hostname`.
+
+| Method | Path | Auth | Request | Success response |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| GET | `/api/session` | – | – | `200 { user: { name, displayName } }`, or `401` when signed out |
+| POST | `/api/signin/options` | – | – | `PublicKeyCredentialRequestOptionsJSON` with `rpId`, `allowCredentials: []`, `userVerification: "preferred"` |
+| POST | `/api/signin/verify` | – | `credential.toJSON()` | `200 { user }` and a session is set. **`404`** if the credential ID is unknown |
+| POST | `/api/register/options` | `flow:"add"` needs a session | `{ flow: "signup", name, displayName }` or `{ flow: "add" }` | `PublicKeyCredentialCreationOptionsJSON` (see below) |
+| POST | `/api/register/verify` | – | `credential.toJSON()` | `200 { user }`. A signup also creates the account and the session |
+| GET | `/api/passkeys` | session | – | `{ rpId, userId, credentials: StoredPasskeyCredential[] }` |
+| PATCH | `/api/passkeys/:id` | session | `{ name }` | `200` updated credential |
+| DELETE | `/api/passkeys/:id` | session + **recent reauth** | – | `200 { success: true }` |
+| PUT | `/api/user` | session + **recent reauth** | `{ name, displayName }` | `{ name, displayName, rpId, userId }` |
+| POST | `/api/reauth/options` | session | – | Request options with `allowCredentials` = the signed-in user's credentials only |
+| POST | `/api/reauth/verify` | session | `credential.toJSON()` | `200` and a short-lived "recently verified" flag is set in the session (for example 5 min). `404` if the credential is unknown. Reject the request if the credential belongs to a different user |
+
+Errors use the shape `{ error: string, message?: string }`. `message` is shown to the user.
+
+## Reauthentication
+
+When an endpoint marked **recent reauth** is called without a fresh
+verification, it must respond with `403 { "error": "reauth_required" }`. The client
+then runs the passkey reauthentication ceremony and retries the request once.
+The server always enforces this check. The client never decides it.
+
+## Registration options
+
+- `rp: { id: RP_ID, name: "The Daily Grind" }`. `rp.id` is required, because the client uses it for Signal API cleanup.
+- `user.id`: a random Base64URL user handle (`passkeyUserId`). `user.name` is the email and `user.displayName` is the name.
+- `excludeCredentials`: the user's existing credentials, including their `transports`.
+- `authenticatorSelection: { residentKey: "required", requireResidentKey: true, userVerification: "preferred" }`. Omit `authenticatorAttachment` so security keys still work.
+- `pubKeyCredParams`: alg `-7` and `-257`.
+- Store the challenge in the session. For `signup`, hold the pending `{ name, displayName }` in the session too, and create the user only after verification succeeds. Reject emails that are already registered.
+- Verify with `requireUserVerification: false` (because the options ask for UV `"preferred"`) and require user presence.
+
+## Stored credential
+
+```ts
+interface StoredPasskeyCredential {
+  id: string;                 // Base64URL credential ID
+  passkeyUserId: string;      // Base64URL user handle
+  credentialPublicKey: string;
+  credentialType: "public-key";
+  credentialDeviceType: "singleDevice" | "multiDevice";
+  credentialBackedUp: boolean;
+  aaguid: string;
+  providerIcon?: string;      // data: URI from the AAGUID registry (UX hint only)
+  name: string;               // AAGUID provider name, or a user-chosen nickname
+  transports: string[];
+  lastUsedAt?: number;        // epoch ms
+  registeredAt: number;       // epoch ms
+  counter: number;
+}
+```
+
+Fill in `name`/`providerIcon` from
+<https://raw.githubusercontent.com/passkeydeveloper/passkey-authenticator-aaguids/refs/heads/main/combined_aaguid.json>.
+Skip the lookup when the AAGUID is all zeros and use "Unknown passkey provider" instead.
+Never use the AAGUID for security decisions.
+
+`GET /api/passkeys` should leave `credentialPublicKey` and `counter` out of its response. The client doesn't need them.
